Package: maluos-agent
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, adduser, python3 (>= 3.12), python3-yaml, maluos-firstboot (>= 0.1.6), maluos-vault (>= 0.3.0), maluos-gateway (>= 0.3.0), maluos-estate (>= 0.3.0)
Description: MaluOS agents as system entities: maluctl agent
 `maluctl agent create` makes an agent real on the host in one step: a
 Linux system user, a MaluDB principal with scope grants, the identity
 mapping the vault and the gateway use, the agent's own secret compartment,
 a gateway policy (class, tiers, cloud, egress ceiling, budget), optionally
 a gateway token delivered as a systemd credential, and a hardened
 maluos-agent@NAME unit running the agent's command as that user with the
 MaluOS endpoints in its environment. `maluctl agent run` executes a
 command as an agent; `remove` reverses it all.
